codex
The initial audit found one avoidable identity weakness: the entry claim duplicated the translated module text manually. I’m tightening Gate A by linking the proof to a `solutionProgram` term whose wrapper is mechanically checked against the generated `solution.mpy`; the entry claim will load that term directly, while the loop circularity still has to match and execute the actual body. This adds a definitional AST constant, not an operational bridge.
apply patch
patch: completed
/workspace/check_program_identity.py
