diff --git a/PROOF.md b/PROOF.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7b0a10021514c2820502e8afbf2cb7beae65c544
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PROOF.md
@@ -0,0 +1,280 @@
+VALIDATED
+
+## What is proven
+
+Under the supplied `MPY` reference semantics, the translated
+`sum_squares` function is partially correct: for every finite semantic list
+`list(VS)`, if the call terminates, its returned integer is
+`sumCeilSquares(VS)`, where
+
+```text
+sumCeilSquares(.ValSeq) = 0
+sumCeilSquares(vCons(V, VS))
+  = ceilF(V) * ceilF(V) + sumCeilSquares(VS)
+```
+
+For finite Python integer and finite binary64-float elements, the supplied
+semantics intends `ceilF` to be `math.ceil`. Thus, conditional on that supplied
+primitive contract, the returned integer is the sum of the squares of the
+elementwise ceilings requested by `prompt.py`.
+
+This is a partial-correctness result in the Kit sense. It is not a separate
+liveness theorem.
+
+## Formal claims
+
+`SPEC.loop-inv` starts at the exact `#loop` generated for the `for` statement.
+The local frame contains only `lst`, `number`, `rounded`, and `total`, with
+plain-function parent `0`. Starting with accumulator `ACC` and remaining
+sequence `VS`, it reaches the same continuation with:
+
+```text
+total = ACC + sumCeilSquares(VS)
+```
+
+The final values of the unobserved loop temporaries `number` and `rounded` are
+existential. `lst`, the frame parent, environment, continuation, and all other
+framed configuration cells are preserved.
+
+`SPEC.sum-squares` starts from the full initial MPY configuration, expands
+`solutionProgram`, loads its definition, resolves and calls `sum_squares` on
+`list(VS)`, executes the function body, and returns
+`sumCeilSquares(VS)`. The result, empty heap, environment, heap location, stack,
+return state, exception state, and exit code are constrained by the claim. The
+post-load module map is intentionally existential because module binding is not
+an observable named by the HumanEval contract.
+
+## Proof-extension inventory
+
+### `solutionProgram`
+
+- Class: definitional summary (a nullary AST constant).
+- Semantic role: names the program AST; it does not replace Python execution.
+- Domain and matched context: the only equation is the nullary term
+  `solutionProgram => Module(...)`, used as the argument of `#loadAll`.
+- Justification scope and containment: `check_program_identity.py` compares the
+  embedded term byte-for-byte, after indentation normalization, with the
+  `solution.mpy` regenerated by the supplied translator.
+- State footprint: none. After expansion, all definition loading, binding,
+  argument evaluation, loop control, and return behavior run under fixed MPY
+  rules.
+- Value/control influence: it selects the complete function body used by the
+  entry claim.
+- Dependents: `SPEC.sum-squares`.
+- Validation: identity check exits 0; the changed-loop-update mutation is
+  rejected with exit 1 and residual result `2` instead of `4`.
+
+### `sumCeilSquares`
+
+- Class: definitional summary.
+- Semantic role: describes the mathematical result; it never appears on the
+  left of an operational configuration rule and does not preempt execution.
+- Domain: all `ValSeq`. The `.ValSeq` and `vCons` equations are disjoint and
+  exhaustive.
+- Termination and consistency: recursion is strictly on the sequence tail;
+  there are no overlapping cases or totalization gaps.
+- State footprint: none.
+- Value influence: fixes the result in both positive claims.
+- Value justification: each cons case is exactly the source loop update after
+  fixed execution reduces `math.ceil(V)` to the supplied `ceilF(V)` and the two
+  integer operations. The theorem remains parametric in the interpretation of
+  the fixed `ceilF` primitive.
+- Dependents: `SPEC.loop-inv` and `SPEC.sum-squares`.
+- Validation: both positive proofs return `#Top`; the false-result mutation is
+  rejected; concrete and differential evidence is recorded below.
+
+### `SPEC.loop-inv`
+
+- Class: derived reachability lemma used coinductively as a loop circularity.
+- Semantic role: reasons about fixed execution; it is not an ordinary rewrite
+  or operational bridge in `verification.k`.
+- Complete match domain: any remaining `VS`, accumulator `ACC`, prior temporary
+  values, environment location `L`, and continuation suffix, with the exact
+  four-key plain local scope and parent `0`; all omitted configuration cells
+  are framed by the generated configuration.
+- Context containment: the claim itself is universally proved over the framed
+  continuation and cells it accepts. The entry claim reaches precisely this
+  loop and scope shape.
+- State footprint: reads the remaining iterator and locals; writes `number`,
+  `rounded`, and `total`; preserves `lst`, environment, parent, continuation,
+  heap, stack, return, exception, and exit state.
+- Value influence: its accumulator result discharges the entry postcondition.
+- Justification: base case uses `sumCeilSquares(.ValSeq) = 0`; the step executes
+  target binding, `math.ceil`, squaring, and accumulation before applying the
+  circularity to the tail.
+- Dependents: `SPEC.sum-squares`.
+- Validation: focused proof and complete-spec proof both print `#Top`; the
+  loop-update mutation and false-result mutation both fail as expected.
+
+There are no proof-local operational bridges, priority rules, result-bearing
+oracles, or simplification axioms.
+
+## Exact commands and actual results
+
+All commands are preserved in `prove.sh`, which was run end-to-end with exit
+status 0.
+
+```bash
+python3 py2mpy.py solution.py > solution.mpy
+python3 check_program_identity.py
+python3 py2mpy.py smoke.py > smoke.mpy
+python3 -m py_compile solution.py smoke.py differential_test.py
+```
+
+Actual identity output:
+
+```text
+program identity: solutionProgram == solution.mpy
+```
+
+All four commands exited 0.
+
+```bash
+kompile --backend llvm reference-semantics/semantics.k \
+  --main-module MPY-KRUN \
+  --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX \
+  --output-definition runtime-kompiled
+krun solution.mpy --definition runtime-kompiled
+krun smoke.mpy --definition runtime-kompiled
+python3 differential_test.py
+```
+
+LLVM compilation exited 0. It emitted only warnings originating in the
+read-only supplied semantics, including its non-exhaustive concrete-function
+warnings. Both `krun` commands exited 0 with final `<k> .K </k>`,
+`<exc> NoExc </exc>`, and semantic exit code 0. `smoke.mpy` executed all five
+prompt examples plus the empty list. Differential output was:
+
+```text
+cases=1008 mismatches=0
+```
+
+```bash
+kompile --backend haskell verification.k \
+  --main-module VERIFICATION \
+  --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX \
+  --output-definition verification-kompiled
+kprove spec.k \
+  --definition verification-kompiled \
+  --spec-module SPEC \
+  --claims SPEC.loop-inv
+kprove spec.k \
+  --definition verification-kompiled \
+  --spec-module SPEC
+```
+
+Actual results:
+
+```text
+kompile: exit 0
+focused loop proof: #Top, exit 0
+complete two-claim proof: #Top, exit 0
+```
+
+The compiler also reported unused-variable warnings in the supplied semantics
+and for intentionally unobserved existential variables in `spec.k`; these do
+not alter the successful exits.
+
+The A5 mutation command was:
+
+```bash
+kprove spec-vacuity.k \
+  --definition verification-kompiled \
+  --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY
+```
+
+Actual result: exit 1 with `WarnStuckClaimState`; the residual `<k>` contains
+`0 ~> .K` while the destination demands `1`.
+
+The body-sensitivity command was:
+
+```bash
+kprove spec-body-mutation.k \
+  --definition verification-kompiled \
+  --spec-module SPEC-BODY-MUTATION
+```
+
+Actual result: exit 1 with `WarnStuckClaimState`; after changing the loop update
+from adding `rounded * rounded` to adding `rounded`, the `[2]` witness leaves
+`2 ~> .K` while the destination demands `4`.
+
+## Gate results
+
+### Gate A — PASS
+
+- A1: `solutionProgram` is mechanically identical to generated
+  `solution.mpy`; its program-defined body executes under fixed semantics. The
+  loop-update mutation is rejected.
+- A2: there are no operational bridges. Fixed execution accounts for all
+  configuration state; the intended observable is the returned integer.
+- A3: lookup, argument evaluation, iterator control, local binding, `ceil`
+  dispatch, and return all execute under MPY. The result-bearing `ceilF` symbol
+  is a supplied external primitive and the theorem is interpretation-parametric
+  in it.
+- A4: both proof-local definitional groups are exhaustive, disjoint, and
+  terminating. No false simplification or rewrite lemma is admitted.
+- A5: the empty input is a realizable witness. The deliberately false result
+  is rejected with residual `0`, proving that the result is constrained and
+  that the claim is non-vacuous.
+
+### Gate B — PASS
+
+- The prompt domain is lists of numbers. The formal `ValSeq` theorem is broader
+  because the supplied semantics declares `ceilF(Val)` total; the intended
+  reading is restricted to integer and finite float elements. This is an
+  explicit over-approximation, not a silently strengthened precondition, and
+  the intended domain is included.
+- K `Int` matches Python's unbounded integers. The concrete K float operations
+  use a 53/11 floating format, matching the finite binary64 values used by
+  CPython and the tests.
+- The summary-to-“ceiling” interpretation is conditional on the supplied
+  `ceilF` contract, and is independently supported by the concrete evidence.
+- The implementation matches all examples, including the negative-float case.
+
+### Gate C — PASS
+
+- The trust ledger below names every unproved boundary and its dependents.
+- Every claimed identity, concrete, differential, mutation, and proof result
+  has an existing artifact and an exact command in `prove.sh`.
+- Formal, conditional, empirical, and excluded conclusions are separated in
+  this report.
+
+## Trust boundary
+
+- `reference-semantics/` is the fixed operational theory trusted by the
+  theorem. All positive claims depend on it; it affects values, state, control,
+  exceptions, and the meaning of termination.
+- `ceilF(Val)` in `reference-semantics/semantics/float.k` is the specific
+  result-bearing trusted primitive. Under symbolic Haskell execution it remains
+  opaque for a symbolic element; concrete rules implement the Int and Float
+  cases for LLVM. Both claims depend on it. The formal theorem proves the fold
+  structure for whatever value this fixed primitive returns; mathematical
+  ceiling is conditional on its supplied contract.
+- `py2mpy.py` is the fixed source-to-constructor translator. It affects program
+  identity. `check_program_identity.py` proves only that the K AST constant
+  equals its generated output, not that the translator is a verified model of
+  all CPython parsing.
+- K v7.1.293, its Haskell/LLVM backends, and their solver/runtime are trusted
+  proof infrastructure.
+
+## Empirically supported facts
+
+`smoke.py` uses LLVM concrete execution for the five prompt examples and the
+empty list; all assertions terminate with `NoExc` and exit code 0.
+
+`differential_test.py` uses an independently constructed ceiling oracle:
+`Fraction(value)` followed by integer numerator/denominator ceiling. It covers
+the prompt examples, empty input, exact integers, values immediately around
+negative and zero boundaries, and 1,000 deterministic random lists drawn from
+400 values in `[-100, 100]`. It reports 1,008 cases and zero mismatches. This is
+finite evidence for the concrete primitive and implementation, not a universal
+equivalence proof.
+
+## Excluded behavior
+
+- Termination as a separate liveness property.
+- CPython behavior for nonnumeric list elements, NaN, infinities, custom
+  numeric classes, or user-defined `__ceil__`.
+- Exceptions or side effects not modeled by the supplied reference semantics.
+- Any theorem that the supplied translator, semantics, K implementation, or
+  solver is itself correct.
diff --git a/check_program_identity.py b/check_program_identity.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..acdaf2913ec33277a19d07b1bdbd02823dd218e2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/check_program_identity.py
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+from pathlib import Path
+import re
+
+
+program_k = Path("program.k").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
+solution_mpy = Path("solution.mpy").read_text(encoding="utf-8").strip()
+
+match = re.search(
+    r"rule solutionProgram =>\n(?P<term>.*?)\nendmodule\n?\Z",
+    program_k,
+    flags=re.DOTALL,
+)
+if match is None:
+    raise AssertionError("program.k does not contain the solutionProgram rule")
+
+embedded = "\n".join(
+    line[4:] if line.startswith("    ") else line
+    for line in match.group("term").splitlines()
+).strip()
+
+if embedded != solution_mpy:
+    raise AssertionError(
+        "solutionProgram differs from solution.mpy\n"
+        f"--- embedded ---\n{embedded}\n"
+        f"--- generated ---\n{solution_mpy}\n"
+    )
+
+print("program identity: solutionProgram == solution.mpy")
diff --git a/differential_test.py b/differential_test.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4589df781d4ef5071dbf8777c9aa33e8c6b25f9a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/differential_test.py
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+from fractions import Fraction
+import random
+
+from solution import sum_squares
+
+
+def independent_ceil(value):
+    fraction = Fraction(value)
+    return -(-fraction.numerator // fraction.denominator)
+
+
+def oracle(values):
+    total = 0
+    for value in values:
+        rounded = independent_ceil(value)
+        total += rounded * rounded
+    return total
+
+
+cases = [
+    [],
+    [1, 2, 3],
+    [1, 4, 9],
+    [1, 3, 5, 7],
+    [1.4, 4.2, 0],
+    [-2.4, 1, 1],
+    [-3.0, -2.0000000000000004, -2.0, -1.9999999999999998],
+    [0.0, -0.0, 0.0000000000000001, -0.0000000000000001],
+]
+
+rng = random.Random(20260725)
+pool = [rng.randint(-10000, 10000) / 100.0 for _ in range(400)]
+for _ in range(1000):
+    length = rng.randint(0, 20)
+    cases.append([rng.choice(pool) for _ in range(length)])
+
+mismatches = []
+for values in cases:
+    actual = sum_squares(values)
+    expected = oracle(values)
+    if actual != expected:
+        mismatches.append((values, actual, expected))
+
+print(f"cases={len(cases)} mismatches={len(mismatches)}")
+if mismatches:
+    raise AssertionError(mismatches[:5])
diff --git a/program.k b/program.k
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..44b2928a51e0ecff6a35f480d3975a65a23c0cf3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/program.k
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+requires "reference-semantics/semantics/syntax.k"
+
+module SOLUTION-PROGRAM
+  imports MPY-SYNTAX
+
+  // This nullary AST constant is checked mechanically against solution.mpy by
+  // check_program_identity.py before compilation.
+  syntax Module ::= "solutionProgram" [function, total]
+  rule solutionProgram =>
+    Module(
+      Import("math")
+      FuncDef("sum_squares", Params("lst"),
+        Assign(Name("total"), Int(0))
+        Assign(Name("number"), Int(0))
+        Assign(Name("rounded"), Int(0))
+        For(Name("number"), Name("lst"),
+          Assign(
+            Name("rounded"),
+            Call(Attribute(Name("math"), "ceil"), Name("number")))
+          AugAssign(
+            Name("total"),
+            "+",
+            BinOp("*", Name("rounded"), Name("rounded"))))
+        Return(Name("total"))))
+endmodule
diff --git a/prove.sh b/prove.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..1e179a35f389d4e27a67bfb4356300c3311a43a3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/prove.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -euo pipefail
+
+python3 py2mpy.py solution.py > solution.mpy
+python3 check_program_identity.py
+python3 py2mpy.py smoke.py > smoke.mpy
+python3 -m py_compile solution.py smoke.py differential_test.py
+
+kompile --backend llvm reference-semantics/semantics.k \
+  --main-module MPY-KRUN \
+  --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX \
+  --output-definition runtime-kompiled
+
+krun solution.mpy --definition runtime-kompiled | tee krun-solution.out
+krun smoke.mpy --definition runtime-kompiled | tee krun-smoke.out
+python3 differential_test.py | tee differential-test.out
+
+kompile --backend haskell verification.k \
+  --main-module VERIFICATION \
+  --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX \
+  --output-definition verification-kompiled
+
+kprove spec.k \
+  --definition verification-kompiled \
+  --spec-module SPEC \
+  --claims SPEC.loop-inv | tee kprove-loop.out
+
+kprove spec.k \
+  --definition verification-kompiled \
+  --spec-module SPEC | tee kprove.out
+
+set +e
+kprove spec-vacuity.k \
+  --definition verification-kompiled \
+  --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY 2>&1 | tee vacuity.out
+vacuity_status=${PIPESTATUS[0]}
+set -e
+if [[ ${vacuity_status} -eq 0 ]]; then
+  echo "ERROR: false-result mutation unexpectedly proved"
+  exit 1
+fi
+echo "EXPECTED FAILURE: false-result mutation exited ${vacuity_status}"
+
+set +e
+kprove spec-body-mutation.k \
+  --definition verification-kompiled \
+  --spec-module SPEC-BODY-MUTATION 2>&1 | tee body-mutation.out
+body_mutation_status=${PIPESTATUS[0]}
+set -e
+if [[ ${body_mutation_status} -eq 0 ]]; then
+  echo "ERROR: changed-body mutation unexpectedly proved"
+  exit 1
+fi
+echo "EXPECTED FAILURE: changed-body mutation exited ${body_mutation_status}"
